# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: vla-entity-property-table-on-demand — extend the entity COM property table as suites actually consume it
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: cad-runtime
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-09-26

* Context

Carried out of =vla-entity-property-bridge= when that P1 closed (its driver,
the SCHMS sigfic suite, is 6/6 headless and pjb confirmed it). The bridge is
a DECLARATIVE table: property name, the entity kinds it applies to, the DXF
group, read-only flag, encoder, decoder. Adding a property is one row plus a
test, which is why the remaining work is small, unglamorous and does NOT
justify keeping a P1 open.

* Why this is demand-driven, deliberately

The obvious next candidates are known — =TrueColor= (group 420), =Closed=
(LWPOLYLINE group 70 bit 1), =MTextAttribute=, and MTEXT =Rotation='s units —
and they are NOT being added speculatively. Two reasons:

- AGENTS.md § /Change Discipline/: no speculative features in a foundational
  module. A row nobody calls is a row nobody has checked against a vendor.
- The mapped subset is supposed to follow what a suite CONSUMES, measured
  (=schms-call-inventory.md= is how the first subset was chosen: 188 ×
  =vla-put-textstring=, 170 × =vla-get-layer=, and so on). A count is a
  better guide than a guess, and it tells us the units and the exact shape
  the caller expects.

So: when a suite fails on =:unknown-com-property=, the property named in that
error is the next row. Until then the table is complete for every consumer we
have.

* How to add one

1. Name the property, the entity kinds, and the DXF group it maps to.
2. Classify it against the dialects FIRST (AGENTS.md § /Dialect Divergence and
   Warnings/): common, extension, resolved divergence, or symmetric
   divergence. =MTEXT Rotation= is the live example — if AutoCAD and BricsCAD
   disagree about radians versus degrees there, that is a divergence to record,
   not a unit to pick.
3. Add the row in =clautolisp/cador/source/vlax-api.lisp=, a read/write
   round-trip test against =entget= at the cador layer, and a line in the
   user manual's entity-properties list.
4. Anything not pinned down by both vendor documents gets a
   =;;; SPEC-UNCERTAIN:= marker and an entry in
   =issues/open/deferred-spec-research.issue= — which now carries the four
   questions the bridge left behind (EffectiveName on dynamic blocks,
   entmakex on BLOCK/ENDBLK, the ENDBLK-terminated entnext walk, TEXT
   bounding-box glyph metrics).

* Acceptance criteria

- No suite fails on =:unknown-com-property= for a property a consumer
  actually calls.
- Every property added carries its dialect classification and a
  round-trip test; unknown properties still raise =:unknown-com-property=
  rather than silently returning nil.

* Demand scan (2026-10-04)

.vla-demand.py over every .lsp / .mnl under /home/claude/src and the
clautolisp tree (1416 files: the corpus, the probes, EPUREE and its SNCF
upstream, outils-autolisp): NO entity property outside the table is called
-- the table is complete for every consumer we have, so nothing is added
(the ticket's own rule). The unmapped names found are all on application /
document objects -- Layouts (vla-item by name), Document.Active,
Preferences.Files.SupportPath, Profiles / ActiveProfile -- called by EPUREE
(comu.lsp) and its SNCF upstream: a different gap, filed as
com-application-object-properties.issue. Stays open, demand-driven.

* Demand scan (2026-10-05)

Re-run after com-application-object-properties closed (2.2.179): 1416 files,
still NO entity property outside the table; every unmapped name is an
application / document property now implemented (ActiveDocument,
SupportPath, Preferences, Files, Layouts, Active, ActiveProfile, Profiles,
Documents). Nothing to add. Note: the scan sees vla-get-* / vla-put-* /
vlax-get[-property] / vlax-put[-property] with a literal name only, not
vlax-invoke methods nor names built at run time. Stays open, demand-driven.
